{"availability":"available","full":"Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris","name":"openai-dev-day-polaris","description":"DemoPilot: turns a project brief into a timed, evidence-aware live demo plan using the OpenAI Decisions API","category":"Developer tools","language":"CSS","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T06:01:48Z","updated":"2026-10-10T08:25:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://openai-dev-day-polaris.vercel.app","topics":["decisions-api","hackathon","openai","react","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://openai-dev-day-polaris.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:57.897Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:57.897Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:57.897Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:57.897Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DemoPilot turns a project brief into a timed live demo plan, with an optional AI review of the lead feature and evidence readiness.","DemoPilot is a presentation coach for hackathon teams and product builders. It helps a presenter decide what to show first, connect claims to visible proof, explain prototype boundaries honestly, and rehearse within a fixed time limit. It does not inspect a repository, run the product being presented, validate market demand, or measure outcomes; the presenter supplies the facts and verifies each claim.","Strong demos are short stories with visible proof. Teams often have a working prototype but struggle to decide what to show, what to say, and how to handle gaps. DemoPilot turns supplied project context into an editable run of show so teams can spend less time staring at a blank page and more time rehearsing the real product."],"features":["45, 60, or 90 second demo outlines","Time-coded instructions for what to show, say, and emphasize","Editable opening hook, script, and closing","Your own evidence and limitations restated next to the plan, with fixed honesty reminders (evidence assessment comes only from the optional AI review)","Limitations section built from your brief, plus a reminder not to imply live data, integrations, or measured impact"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5955d5b84729745d5a7abf622dcbfa4baa49523584b2c86ed575b885fccc1f26","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:58.044Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:58.044Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"DemoPilot turns a project brief into a timed live demo plan, with an optional AI review of the lead feature and evidence readiness.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Browser local storage holds draft data; there is no account or cloud synchronization.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"No login, cloud sync, team collaboration, project/repository inspection, evidence capture, or server-side brief storage.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"AI review requires an operator-configured API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5955d5b84729745d5a7abf622dcbfa4baa49523584b2c86ed575b885fccc1f26","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:58.045Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T08:25:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yash-1706/openai-dev-day-polaris/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:58.045Z","hash":"5955d5b84729745d5a7abf622dcbfa4baa49523584b2c86ed575b885fccc1f26","originalBytes":18055,"storedBytes":18055,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","brief","key